   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/Tensors/RealTensor/Vector/VolumeForm.lean",
   "fix": "Close it through the explicit lemmas instead: `congr 1; ext i j; simp [Module.Basis.toMatrix_apply, basisFin4, Module.Basis.repr_reindex_apply, Lorentz.Vector.basis_repr_apply]` (the same `Module.Basis.toMatrix_apply` route the file already uses at line 148). If the `rfl` is kept deliberately, add a comment stating which defeq it relies on, as was done for the `change` at line 144.",
   "issue": "After `rw [volumeForm, _root_.neg_apply, Module.Basis.det_apply, neg_inj]` the remaining goal is `(basisFin4.toMatrix v).det = (Matrix.of fun i j => v j (finSumFinEquiv.symm i)).det`, closed by a bare undocumented `rfl`. That holds only by unfolding `Basis.reindex` (`Finsupp.domLCongr`), `Basis.repr`, and `Pi.basisFun`'s `ofEquivFun`; Physlib itself does not treat `basis.repr p \u03bc = p \u03bc` as `rfl` (`Vector/Basic.lean:296` proves `basis_repr_apply` by `simp`/`rw [Pi.basisFun_repr]`), so any propositionally-equal re-definition of `Lorentz.Vector.basis` upstream silently breaks this proof while the stated lemma stays true.",
   "line": 96
  }
